  "equipment_type": "Power and energy meter",
  "applies_to": "Eaton IQ 250 and IQ 260 electronic power meters on Modbus, read by a BASgatewayLX.",
  "summary": "Gateway profile for the Eaton IQ 250/260: 168 Analog Inputs, 27 polled by default (voltages, currents, W/VAR/VA, PF and frequency). Energy, demand, THD and min/max values are in the profile but unpolled.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "Built from Contemporary Controls' BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile Eaton_IQ_250_260_bLX.csv; the profile maps the registers in the maker's Modbus register document (https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/IQ250.pdf).",
    "Object instances are the ones this profile assigns when it is loaded into the gateway. A site that edited or rebuilt the profile may use different instances.",
    "Only 27 of the 168 rows are flagged for polling in the profile; the rest are served only after you tick them in the gateway. Their descriptions say \"not polled by default\".",
    "The CSV has no read/write column: Analog/Binary Inputs are read-only and Analog/Binary Outputs are commandable (priority array), which is how the gateway maps them (access inferred). Descriptions give the Modbus register each object reads.",
    "Some names appear more than once in the profile as published (Uncompensated VAR-hours Positive); they are kept as printed and told apart by instance."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile Eaton_IQ_250_260",
    "doc_number": "Eaton_IQ_250_260_bLX.csv",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/Eaton_IQ_250_260.zip"
  },
